MyGo patch 0013 (VoxtNew): a tooltip takes Escape only when no other
overlay does.

A tooltip is an overlay built inside the overlay that shows its anchor,
so it is on top of a dialog or popover and took the Escape meant to
close it: with the keyboard focus on a button with a tip (a dialog's ×,
an ⓘ), the first Escape hid the tip and only the second closed the
dialog. routeKey now gives a key to a tooltip's OverlayShortcut only
when no other overlay registered it; the tip goes with the dialog. A tip
over the window alone still hides on Escape (TestTooltipLetsDialogClose,
TestTooltipFocus).

